T:Native Land Waltz
% NFF Book 2016
S:collected from Kath McCaughey, Grafton, NSW
S:collected by Dave de Hugard, 1987
H:The song itself pays tibute to the Free Selection Acts of the 1860's which 
H:allowed individuals to select and acquire tracts of Crown land for farming purposes,
N:Other versions were collected in Australia from:
N:- Stan Treacy, by Brad Tate & Dave de Hugard, as "Flora's Waltz"
N:- Rita Baker, by John Meredith as "Mum's Waltz" & as "Rita Baker's Mum's Waltz", https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/12025
N:- Clem O'Neales, by Dave de Hugard, as "Hughie's Waltz"
N:- Bill Brennan, New England, by Barry McDonald as "Give Me a Hut in my own Native land", https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/5055241
N:- Bill Cooper, Parkes, by Rob Willis as "Bill Cooper's Waltz"
N:- Bill Berry, Lithgow, by Alex Hood, as "A Hut in my own Native Land"  https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/3101883
N:- Cotter Family, Binalong, by John Meredith & Rob Willis, as "Give Me a Hut in my own Native land"  https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/1417074
N:- Jim Lowe, Guyra, by Barry McDonald, as "Give Me A Hut", https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/653451,
N:- Clarrie Gates, Balladoran, NSW, By the Bush Music Club as the "Balladoran Waltz". 
